      "name": "Jiří Šír",
      "created_at": "2024-02-21T22:52:44.187Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi,<br>\nI have written small code workaround here:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"115884\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/keyur_paraskar/48/53644_2.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/migrated-data-made-the-custom-doctypes-in-the-new-bench-unedittable/115884/3\">Migrated Data made the custom Doctypes in the new bench unedittable</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/framework/app-development/24\"><span data-category-id=\"24\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #0E76BD; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #F7941D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"5\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --has-parent\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">App Development</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/nasir_khan\">@Nasir_Khan</a>, Thanks for the prompt response! Setting the developer mode on fixed the issue with server scripts discrepencies. Although I still get the following error when trying to edit an existing custom doctype. \n <a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/3/b/3b8e82ba522033b52e6d8094a7bd1a93c3bc97a2.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/3b8e82ba522033b52e6d8094a7bd1a93c3bc97a2\" title=\"Screenshot\">[Screenshot]</a>\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n\n<p>I hope it helps.<br>\nJiri Sir</p>",
